---
import { HOW_THIS_WORKS } from '../../lib/learning/policy';
---

<section aria-labelledby="how-it-works" class="how-it-works card">
  <h2 id="how-it-works" class="card-h">
    How this works
  </h2>
  <div class="hw-cols">
    <div class="hw-col">
      {HOW_THIS_WORKS.map((p) => (
        <p>{p}</p>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="hw-col">
      <h3>The three pieces, in plain words</h3>
      <dl>
        <dt>Knowledge tracing (BKT)</dt>
        <dd>
          For each idea the site keeps one number: how likely it is that you know it. A correct answer nudges
          the number up, a wrong answer nudges it down, and a lucky guess or a slip is allowed for. An idea
          counts as mastered when that number reaches 95%. The starting guesses (30% known, 10% chance to
          learn at each step, 10% slip, 20% guess) are common defaults, not measurements of you. Source:
          <a href="/references/#S-037">Corbett and Anderson (1994)</a>.
        </dd>
        <dt>Spaced review (SM-2)</dt>
        <dd>
          After you answer, each question gets a date to come back: tomorrow, then in 6 days, then each gap
          about 2.5 times longer while you keep getting it right. A wrong answer, or "I am not sure", brings
          it back tomorrow. Source: <a href="/references/#S-038">Wozniak (1990)</a>.
        </dd>
        <dt>Choosing the next item (Thompson sampling)</dt>
        <dd>
          The site tries six kinds of action and slowly favours the ones that seem to help you, with a little
          randomness so it keeps checking the others. Source: <a href="/references/#S-039">Thompson (1933)</a>
          .
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
        <strong>Heuristic, not a test.</strong> None of this is a grade or a measurement of ability. It is a
        coach that makes suggestions, and you can ignore it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>It stays on your device.</strong> Your answers, estimates and streak are saved in this browser
        only. Nothing is uploaded, and there is no account, unless you switch on optional sync, which exists
        only on builds that have it configured and is described on the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.
        You can export, import or erase everything on the <a href="/progress/">progress page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
